  "local_patch_scope": "Compression comparisons are in driven brane. The enriched patch has all its outer boundaries held. Zero-displacement/legacy-field energy is the common stored offset for this diagnostic. Force divided by the discrete displacement norm, stretches and volume ratios use actual values. The global wall and ordinary lattice sites outside the patch are held. The re-equilibrated local patch is separate from the saved solid used for the virtual-work and closed-shell comparisons.",
  "clamp_extension_control": "The clamp-only archive is a diagnostic extension which holds original nonterminal solid nodes while carrying the adjoining fluid. Under virtual motion those two extensions can slip on a tilted bank. The physical bookkeeping reported in the main text uses the bond archive; disk and complementary motions sum to the same field and material translation on the sidewall. No reaction from the mismatched extension is attributed to a permanently bonded wall.",
